hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28109","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Fudayl meaning Ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, he said: I heard Talhah ibn Ubaydillah ibn Kurayz, he said: I heard Umm al-Darda say: I heard Abu al-Darda say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is answered for a man in his absence for his brother, so whenever he supplicates for his brother with a supplication, the angel says: And for you the like."
"28110","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Malik informed us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Safwan ibn Abdillah, and under him was Umm al-Darda, and he came to them and found Umm al-Darda, and she said to him: Do you intend Hajj this year? He said: Yes. She said: Supplicate for us with good, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The supplication of the Muslim man is answered for his brother in his absence, at his head is an angel entrusted with him, whenever he supplicates for his brother with good he says: Amin, and for you the like. He said: So I went out to the market and met Abu al-Darda, and he narrated to me on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of that."
